<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of weekend</p>
<p>matches in the Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro soccer</p>
<p>championships:</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> America-S.J.Rio Preto   0   Sao Jose			2</p>
<p> Aracatuba		   2   Portuguesa-Santista	 0</p>
<p> Guarani		     1   Botafogo-Ribeirao Preto   0</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira   2   Rio Branco		    1</p>
<p> Juventus		    3   Portuguesa		    3</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		  1   Sao Paulo		     1</p>
<p> Palmeiras		   2   Santos			  0</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	    0   Corinthians		   1</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group one</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 6  4  2  0 21  6 14</p>
<p> Guarani		   6  4  2  0 16 10 14</p>
<p> Santos		    6  3  1  2  9  8 10</p>
<p> Portuguesa		6  2  2  2 15 13  8</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  6  2  2  2 10 13  8</p>
<p> Botafogo		  6  0  4  2  5  7  4</p>
<p> Juventus		  6  0  3  3  7 15  3</p>
<p> America		   6  0  2  4  5 16  2</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     6  4  2  0 10  5 14</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 6  3  3  0 13  5 12</p>
<p>Internacional Limeira 6  3  2  1  8  6 11</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 6  2  1  3  7  7  7</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		6  1  4  1  7  7  7</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   6  2  0  4  6 11  6</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  6  1  1  4  4  8  4</p>
<p> Rio Branco		6  1  1  4  6 12  4</p>
<p>Note: the teams play once against the teams from their own</p>
<p>group and then twice against the teams in the opposite group.</p>
<p>The top two teams in each group then qualify for the four-team</p>
<p>final stage.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, first stage</p>
<p> America		     1   Americano		     1</p>
<p> Barreira		    0   Flamengo			5</p>
<p> Botafogo		    4   Itaperuna		     2</p>
<p> Madureira		   2   Volta Redonda		 0</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	     1   Fluminense		    0</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	 7  6  1  0 13  3 19</p>
<p> Botafogo		5  5  0  0 17  6 15</p>
<p> Flamengo		5  4  1  0 15  2 13</p>
<p> Madureira	     5  3  0  2  7  3  9</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	 6  2  2  2 10 11  8</p>
<p> America		 5  1  4  0  4  3  7</p>
<p> Fluminense	    5  2  1  2  7  8  7</p>
<p> Americano	     7  2  1  4  7 10  7</p>
<p> Bangu		   4  1  1  2  5  6  4</p>
<p> Itaperuna	     6  1  0  5  4 13  3</p>
<p> Olaria		  5  0  1  4  3  9  1</p>
<p> Barreira		6  0  0  6  3 21  0</p>
<p>Note: The tournament is divided into three stages. The</p>
<p>winners of each qualify for the final play-off stage. Only the</p>
<p>top eight teams in the first stage continue into the second</p>
<p>stage and only the top six in the second stage carry on into</p>
<p>the third.</p>
